  "function_code": 168,
  "name": "Interpolator",
  "description": "The interpolator function code outputs a value determined by a two dimensional linear interpolation of the two inputs. The coordinates of the values within a defined five-by-five table are the basis of the interpolation. If either input is outside the table, the first output becomes the largest possible number. The second output is a boolean value that indicates if the input points are in the five-by-five table range. If either input is outside the table, the second output becomes a one.",
  "description_lines": [
    "The interpolator function code outputs a value determined by",
    "a two dimensional linear interpolation of the two inputs. The",
    "coordinates of the values within a defined five-by-five table are",
    "the basis of the interpolation. If either input is outside the",
    "table, the first output becomes the largest possible number.",
    "The second output is a boolean value that indicates if the",
    "input points are in the five-by-five table range. If either input is",
    "outside the table, the second output becomes a one."
  ],
